I just checked really quickly, so I'll show you that.

00:57.360 --> 01:00.920
And before we do, I wanted to kind of share some experience with you.

01:01.000 --> 01:04.420
Just some experience that I've learned from studying and been doing this a long time.

01:04.600 --> 01:06.580
Because a lot of people are in a lot of pain right now.

01:06.680 --> 01:11.340
A lot of people are questioning their own reality because the mind loves to torture you.

01:11.520 --> 01:18.440
There's a well-documented phenomenon where investors feel more pain from missing a move than they do from actually losing money.

01:18.660 --> 01:22.700
And so I wanted to kind of just tell you about this in case you're unfamiliar with it.

01:22.700 --> 01:27.740
Because I am getting a lot of comments like this where people are saying they're in pain or it sucks or whatever else.

01:27.920 --> 01:30.520
And frankly, it's kind of wild if you think about it.

01:30.700 --> 01:36.920
Because it wasn't even that long ago, a month and a half ago, people were trolling me for not selling the spot Bitcoin, right?

01:36.960 --> 01:41.320
And now all of a sudden, I bet there's a lot of people that would willingly trade places with me.

01:41.440 --> 01:44.040
I often talk about you don't need to be right or wrong, okay?

01:44.060 --> 01:44.740
That's just ego.

01:44.940 --> 01:46.320
It's about making money, right?

01:46.320 --> 01:52.140
I often talk about how you can be right and still lose money or you can be flat wrong and still do okay and still profit.

01:52.560 --> 01:57.300
I often talk about positioning for every single possible outcome all at the same time.

01:57.460 --> 02:02.540
So that if something insane happens, okay, you can have at least some exposure to the move, right?

02:02.560 --> 02:03.700
Which keeps the FOMO away.

02:03.860 --> 02:06.640
It allows you to maintain some level of neutrality.

02:06.640 --> 02:12.580
And more importantly, being different towards the money so that you can actually apply critical thinking

02:12.580 --> 02:16.580
and deal with the things that are going to happen outside of your expectations.

02:16.820 --> 02:19.140
And let me break it to you in case you haven't figured this out.

02:19.240 --> 02:23.140
Things are going to happen outside your expectations in this game all the time, okay?

02:23.320 --> 02:27.500
Yes, you can go on a nice hot streak where you seem to apparently not be able to lose for a while.

02:27.660 --> 02:29.700
But do not confuse that with skill, right?

02:30.000 --> 02:32.340
Sometimes everything seems to go your way.

02:32.460 --> 02:35.660
And other times, things will happen outside of your expectation.

02:35.660 --> 02:37.380
And you have to be aware of that.

02:37.440 --> 02:38.720
You have to be able to deal with that.

02:39.000 --> 02:44.760
And more importantly, you have to focus your mental energy in places that is conducive to doing better.

02:44.900 --> 02:48.000
And that's why I wanted to talk about this because I know a lot of people are hurting right now.

02:48.060 --> 02:48.980
I understand that.

02:49.020 --> 02:53.600
But they're hurting because their brains don't work, which I understand is quite an autistic thing to say.

02:54.000 --> 02:55.880
But you can see what I've typed into Google up here.

02:56.020 --> 02:58.160
And this is the psychology of regret.

02:58.680 --> 03:03.920
Missing a major market move often inflicts deeper psychological wounds than losing money

03:03.920 --> 03:07.960
because it triggers a potent mix of counterfactual thinking and identity failure.

03:08.340 --> 03:10.020
Why missing out hurts more?

03:10.480 --> 03:11.780
Imagined futures, okay?

03:11.860 --> 03:17.780
There's unbounded scenarios that you could create in your mind about how much your life could have been better

03:17.780 --> 03:24.320
or what car you could have been driving or what wife you could have upgraded to had you have hit that hundred bagger.

03:24.480 --> 03:27.140
And this, of course, amplifies the pain of unrealized gains.

03:27.380 --> 03:28.260
Personal blame, right?

03:28.260 --> 03:31.040
And this trade feels like a personal failure of judgment.

03:31.360 --> 03:35.400
Oh, how much I suck for not buying the picot bottom of a market.

03:35.540 --> 03:39.780
And I'm sure, going back to what I said about you could be right and still not make any money.

03:39.900 --> 03:41.640
How many people have done this?

03:41.660 --> 03:44.460
I'm sure we probably all have if you've been in markets any length of time at all.

03:44.740 --> 03:46.000
I know I've done this several times.

03:46.300 --> 03:49.440
How many people have gotten to a bottom and thought to yourself,

03:49.760 --> 03:52.060
I'm pretty sure this is the bottom, but I'm not going to buy.

03:52.160 --> 03:55.340
And then you watch the market rally and you're like, oh, I'm like a deer in the headlights now.

03:55.400 --> 03:56.180
I don't know how to act.

03:56.180 --> 03:57.700
I don't know how to buy a high or low pullback.

03:57.760 --> 03:58.360
I don't know what to do.

03:58.660 --> 04:02.100
And instead of look for a nice high probability low to get in on,

04:02.320 --> 04:05.180
we start going, oh, man, how much money would I have made?

04:05.200 --> 04:06.720
Let me calculate this, right?

04:06.760 --> 04:10.660
I would have had five wives instead of the one I got that doesn't respect me, right?

04:11.800 --> 04:14.020
I'm being kind of silly here, as you can tell.

04:14.100 --> 04:20.100
But it's very easy, isn't it, to imagine this scenario where the only reason you're not in a super yacht right now

04:20.100 --> 04:23.100
is because you missed the Bitcoin bottom by 20K so far.

04:23.100 --> 04:27.860
And there is no sense in holding this as a personal failure because let me break it to you as well.

04:28.140 --> 04:31.080
You're going to not hit every bottom from now on, okay?

04:31.220 --> 04:33.820
No matter how much you think you can learn from what's just happened,

04:34.280 --> 04:36.600
assuming the bottom actually was in, okay?

04:36.660 --> 04:40.460
If you didn't buy it, trust me, it's not going to be the last time you miss a bottom, okay?

04:40.620 --> 04:42.700
And it's not going to be the last time you miss a top either.

04:42.940 --> 04:45.620
There is no possible way to catch every bottom and top.

04:45.620 --> 04:49.600
And I know social media and YouTubers love to convince you otherwise,

04:49.760 --> 04:53.000
that they can buy every bottom and sell every top, but they can't, okay?

04:53.140 --> 04:54.800
And you have to come to terms with that.

04:54.920 --> 04:55.860
Which brings into this, right?

04:55.920 --> 04:56.600
Social comparison.

04:57.040 --> 05:00.560
Watching your peers profit triggers intense exclusion anxiety.

05:00.920 --> 05:03.920
I will say this seems, to me at least, to be a bit of a sheepish thing,

05:04.000 --> 05:05.860
but I guess a lot of people are sheepish.

05:06.100 --> 05:08.660
So, but again, this is very low vibrational thinking.

05:08.880 --> 05:11.080
Oh, everyone around me is making money and I'm not.

05:11.080 --> 05:14.500
Or why can't I just be happy for people that got it right, you know?

05:14.720 --> 05:18.400
